{
    "background_story": "Anderson was a rugged outdoorsman who spent most of his life working on the railways. His nickname 'The Shoveler' was earned from his tireless efforts to clear snow from the tracks during the harsh Canadian winters. With a shovel in hand, Anderson would brave the blizzards, ensuring the trains kept running on schedule. His dedication and strength in the face of adversity earned him the respect of his colleagues and the gratitude of the communities he served. Anderson's work was not just about clearing snow; it was about keeping families connected, goods moving, and the economy thriving. Even in retirement, Anderson's legacy as 'The Shoveler' lived on, inspiring a new generation of railway workers to follow in his footsteps.",
